(Included by 340_thing_see.vox. Plan 310 §3: a structure defined in one file
 is usable from another via `see` - the definition is parsed into the program
 the way a function definition is, so `point` is a type noun on the far side
 of the boundary, and the manifest it declares travels with it.)

A thing called point has
  a function called 'placed at',
  a number called x is 0,
  a number called y is 0.

To do the point's 'placed at', with a number called x and a number called y.
  a point called plotted.
  Set plotted's x to x.
  Set plotted's y to y.
  Return a point, plotted.

(An ordinary global function taking a point first, so the including file can
 reach it through the instance possessive as well as by name.)
To 'shifted east' with a point called start.
  Set start's x to start's x add 1.
  Return a point, start.
